  "narrative": "Compared to last week's sale, not enough feeder cattle for a true market test. Feeder Cattle defiantly showed a higher undertone with good buyer demand for fresh calves coming off grass. Slaughter Cows traded 2.00-3.00 higher, Cows returning to feed sold firm on a heavy run with good demand for young feeding cows. Supply included: 24% Feeder Cattle (48% Steers, 41% Heifers, 11% Bulls); 48% Slaughter Cattle (88% Cows, 12% Bulls); 28% Replacement Cattle (65% Stock Cows, 21% Bred Cows, 0% Bred Heifers, 13% Open Heifers, 1% Cow-Calf Pairs). Feeder cattle supply over 600 lbs was 32%.",
